nge of  evolve columns  so why use disposable  personally it's worth defining what we  mean by disposable  many companies are moving towards  disposable solutions  for greater productivity and efficiency  as well as moving towards single use and  flexible facilities  disposables also mitigate the  bottlenecks in downstream process areas  there are a range of disposal items  available for manufacturers  to use from tubing connectors  buffer and product bags and the list  goes on  these items are usually low cost and are  easily replaced  as long as the supplier and the supply  chains well established  columns on the other hand are inherently  more costly  due to the engineering required and also  the  resin contained within therefore  disposable columns are becoming more  prevalent  but are potentially not single use but  more  campaign use the benefits  of disposable columns are plenty  including  operational speed as in they're  essentially plug and play  and negates the need for additional  facility space  in-house expertise and labor time for  column packing  and qualification as well as cleaning  and validation disposable  disposable columns provide operational  flexibility  and rapid change over with reduced line  clearance issues  due to the nature of disposable columns  usually  not required to be larger than about say  30 centimeters  they're more adapted for the increasing  continuous column chromatography market  and also supports alternative  personalized therapies  i.e smaller scale fermentation batches  and column requirements  sprayer wanted to complement its  absorbance with a column  and in collaboration with delta again  supplying the evolve column  the evolve column range is an easy to  use  cost effective and ready to use pilot to  process scale columns  we currently offer seven different sizes  including a 7  10 14 20  25 35 and now 45 centimeter diameter  columns  which all have a non-metallic flow path  the columns conform to the relevant  regulatory requirements  for manufacture and they are rated to  four bar operational  we call the columns the evolve columns  as although we wanted to provide the  customers with a  standard operational column we added a  semi-disposable twist  this is what we call the refresh kit  this kit allows the customer to replace  the full wetted flow path whilst  retaining the column skeleton  this not only reduces waste but also  reduces the cost as the refresh kit  to replace is approximately one-third of  the price of the column  however to further support our customers  you could say that we evolved and  developed a fully disposable  column  tray developed lab scale columns with  our evolv  r range which are standing for research  the evolv r range is a 5 and 50 ml  column  and scales well to our development pilot  or process scale columns  which is the evolve d d referring to  disposable  both the evolve r and d columns have  many similar features  highlighted on this slide as mentioned  the evolver columns are 5 and 50 mil  with a  0.5 and 5 centimeters cross-sectional  area  and a fixed bed height of 10 centimeters  our evolve d range however has a column  diameter  of 7 10 or 20 centimeters  and comes in three different bed heights  of 5  10 or 20 centimeters  this covers a column volume range from  approximately 200 mils  to 6.3 liters  as with the evolve range the evolve d  columns can be used with all common  process solutions  and are rated to 4 bar operational use  disposable evolve columns demonstrate  good scalability  in this example we use etoxiclear  our endotoxin removal absorbent  we loaded a comparable amount of igg  solution  containing endotoxin onto each column  to about 20 mix per ml  of its orbit as  etoxicly works in a negative mode with  the igg product  passing through the column and the  endotoxin is being retained  the flow-through material for all three  columns  formats exhibit high recoveries of igg  and demonstrated greater than four and a  half log clearance of endotoxin  to below 0.1 endotoxin units per meg of  igg  it is worth noting that in this case the  5 ml column demonstrated slightly lower  recoveries  due to a minor discrepancy in  approaching concentration determination  the evolved d columns can can be  provided with a sorry  the evolved e columns can be provided  with a range of our in-house products  like oxyclear which i just described  but it can also be used as a platform  technology for a range of other  absorbents and resins from other  suppliers  the evolve d columns have been ista  tested  on all our column sizes and have  demonstrated mechanical stability  in preservative kept in cold storage for  up to  two years as well as column efficiency  stability  bioburden and endotoxin testing has been  performed to demonstrate that the column  does not present itself with any dead  spaces  and has good clearance the evolved  columns can be provided as either a  non-gmp version  or gmp-ready pre-packed in our iso 7  clean room environment at our isle of  man facility  all the gmp ready columns come provided  with bioburden and endotoxin testing  with certificates analysis and a full  regulatory support file  developed and delivered to you ready to  use  in addition to the current evolve r and  d range  astray are continuing to expand our  product range  for initial scout work australia provide  our ht1 and 5 columns  which are a simple proven design column  of 1 and 5  mil and we're also looking to bridge the  gap  between our evolve r and d columns with  our  new range of 100 and 200 ml columns  the evolve s additionally  we are listening to our customers and  we're planning to increase our evolve d  column range  with a 15 centimeter bed height as well  as larger diameter evolve d columns  now in summary disposable solutions well  the markets are moving towards this  for ease flexibility and resolving the  issues faced with conventional  chromatography our evolve column  a semi-disposable column with a refresh  kit  has been evolved into a pre-packed  validated fully disposable column  evolve d the evolve d comes in a range  of  sizes and bed heights and provides a  cost-effective ready-to-use column  the evolv r and evolve d column range is  ideal suited to  toxic clear as well as our other  adsorbents allowing for excellent  protein recoveries  whilst providing high clearance of  endotoxin  to levels below 0.1 eu per mig as  demonstrated  the evolved d columns have a  non-metallic flow path like  our evolved columns and are constructed  from pharmaceutical grade material  making them suitable for the  biomanufacturing market  evolved columns have been established to  be a platform for pre-packed gmp ready  columns  for a range of in-house and customer  adsorbents and resins  and we are expanding our range with our  smaller scouting columns  of one and five mil our 100 and 200 mil  evolve s and our different evolve d  sizes  thank you for your valuable time and  attention i'll now take any questions  you may have  and of course if you think of any  additional questions after this webinar  or want to learn more about australia by  separations please don't hesitate  to contact us or visit our website at  www.australbiasoperations.com  thank you  that's great buzz thanks very much for  that presentation just to remind  everyone  if you do have any questions you can use  the chat function  which is currently available and we'll  try and get to your questions  we've got a few questions that have come  through in the meantime buzz  first one asks about the pressure flow  characteristics  of our prepack columns have we done any  work in terms of flow pressure curves  and how do they compare to other sorts  of typical process columns  so we've done uh flow curves obviously  on our empty columns  and they're uh they're very good  obviously  we have um for our  smaller seven and ten evolve d columns  are a three mil id port and for our  larger  20 centimeter